{"G1006":{"id":"G1006","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1006","disambiguated_id":"G1006 =","unique_id":"G1006","headword":"βόσκω","transliteration":"boskō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to feed","definition_en":"βόσκω, \n [in LXX for רעה ;] \nprop., of a herdsman, to feed: Mat.8:33, Mrk.5:14, Luk.8:34 15:15; metaphorically, of Christian pastoral care, Jhn.21:15, 17. Pass., of cattle, to feed, graze: Mat.8:30, Mrk.5:11, Luk.8:32.†\n SYN.: ποιμαίνειν, to tend, shepherd, a wider term, including oversight as well as feeding (see Tr., Syn., §xxv). (AS)","source_line":1128}],"occurrence_count":9,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"pastando","count":3},{"gloss":"alimenta","count":2},{"gloss":"porcos","count":1},{"gloss":"que-apascentavam","count":1},{"gloss":"cuidavam-porcos","count":1},{"gloss":"alimentar","count":1}]},"G1867":{"id":"G1867","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1867","disambiguated_id":"G1867 =","unique_id":"G1867","headword":"ἐπαινέω","transliteration":"epaineō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to praise","definition_en":"ἐπ-αινέω, -ῶ \n [in LXX for הָלַל pi., שָׁבַח pi. ;] \nto praise: with accusative, Rom.15:11, 1Co.11:22; before ὅτι, Luk.16:8, 1Co.11:2; absol., before ὅτι, 1Co.11:17.†\n (AS)","source_line":2008}],"occurrence_count":6,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"louvo","count":3},{"gloss":"celebrai","count":1},{"gloss":"elogiarei","count":1},{"gloss":"elogio","count":1}]},"G2207":{"id":"G2207","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2207","disambiguated_id":"G2207 =","unique_id":"G2207","headword":"ζηλωτής","transliteration":"zēlōtēs","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-T","gloss_en":"zealot","definition_en":"ζηλωτής, -οῦ, ὁ\n (ζηλόω), [in LXX for קַנָּא (θεὸς ζ.), Exo.20:5 34:14, Deu.4:24 5:9 6:15; קַנּוֹא, Nam.1:2 (θεός); pl., I Est.8:72; ζ. τῶν νόμων, 2Ma.4:2;τὸν ζ. Φινεές, 4Ma.18:12 (cf. Num.25:11)* ;] \n__1. in cl. an emulator, zealous admirer (Plat., al.). \n __2. eagerly desirous, zealous; \n __(a) absol., as in OT, ll. with; \n __(b) with genitive obj.: (zealous to acquire or to defend), 1Co.14:12, Tit.2:14, 1Pe.3:13; τ. νόμου (2Mac, l.with), Act.21:20; παραδόσεων, Gal.1:14; with genitive of person(s), θεοῦ, Act.22:3. \n __3. In FlJ, NT, a Zealot, member of the Jewish party so called: as surname of the Apostle Simon, Luk.6:15, Act.1:13.†\n (AS)","source_line":2351}],"occurrence_count":8,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"zelosos","count":3},{"gloss":"zeloso","count":3},{"gloss":"Zelote","count":2}]},"G2280":{"id":"G2280","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2280","disambiguated_id":"G2280 = a Name of","unique_id":"G2455G","headword":"Θαδδαῖος","transliteration":"Thaddaios","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Thaddaeus","definition_en":"Θαδδαῖος, -ου, ὁ (Aram. תּדִאַי, תַּדַּי), \n Thaddæus: Mat.10:3, Mrk.3:18 (WH, mg., Λεββαῖος, which see).†\n (AS)","source_line":2429}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Tadeu","count":2}]},"G2933":{"id":"G2933","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2933","disambiguated_id":"G2933 =","unique_id":"G2933","headword":"κτῆμα","transliteration":"ktēma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"possession","definition_en":"κτῆμα, -τος, τό\n (κτάομαι), [in LXX for כֶּרֶם, etc. ;] \na possession, property: Mat.19:22, Mrk.10:22, Act.2:45 5:1.†\n (AS)","source_line":3128}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"bens","count":1},{"gloss":"propriedades","count":1},{"gloss":"vendiam-propriedades-bens","count":1},{"gloss":"propriedade","count":1}]},"G3576":{"id":"G3576","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3576","disambiguated_id":"G3576 =","unique_id":"G3576","headword":"νωθρός","transliteration":"nōthros","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"dull","definition_en":"νωθρός, -ά, -όν \n [in LXX: Pro.22:29 (חָשֹׁךְ), Sir.4:29 11:12 * ;] \nsluggish, slothful: Heb.5:11 6:12 (for similar usage in π., see MM, xvii). \n SYN.: ἀργός (which see), βραδύς (AS)","source_line":